# README & Documentation Policy

`README.md` is the user-facing guide and the codebase map for this Flask app. After creating, renaming, deleting, or meaningfully changing a module, route, env var, or user-visible feature, update `README.md` in the same turn before finishing.

Do not invent new top-level sections. Fit changes into the existing headings. Do not add Getting Started, Changelog, or Recent Updates.

## When You Must Update

Update README when any of these happen:
- New / renamed / deleted Python module under `app/` (or `app.py`)
- New page, route, or user-visible capability (inbox, tags, sync, search, Groq, etc.)
- Changed login, IMAP connect, or multi-account flow
- New or renamed environment variable
- Changed run command, Python deps, or Groq fallback behavior

Skip README for typos, private refactors with no behavior/API change, CSS-only polish, or graphify-out updates.

## Section Map

| Change type | Update these README sections |
|---|---|
| User-visible capability (sync, tags, search, digest, hide, respond-now) | **Features** |
| venv, `pip install`, `flask --app app run`, debug host/port | **Run Locally** |
| Per-user vs server Groq key, heuristic fallback, model discovery | **Adding a Groq API Key** |
| IMAP login, App Passwords, host auto-fill, adding accounts | **Connecting Your Inbox** |
| New/renamed/removed env var | **Environment Variables** |
| New/renamed/deleted file or folder | **Project Structure** |

Refresh the Features bullets so they match what the app actually does (IMAP multi-account, SQLite + FTS, categories, Groq-or-heuristic summaries, digest, search, `.eml`/`.mbox` import, tags, hidden mail, Respond Now). Do not leave the tree describing only login/dashboard/upload if those other pages exist.

## Project Structure entries

Keep the tree one-line role comments:

```
app/routes.py                   All HTTP routes (login, inbox, dashboard, search, accounts, tags, settings)
app/services/store.py           SQLite persistence, FTS, accounts, tags, settings
```

If a file moves, move its README line; do not leave a stale duplicate.

## Writing Rules

- Document behavior and contracts, not commit history.
- Use exact file and env names with backticks (`GROQ_API_KEY`, `EmailStore`).
- One sentence per tree line; put detail in Features or the matching how-to section.
- Preserve heading depth and tone of adjacent sections.

## Done Checklist

- Features bullets still true
- Project Structure tree line added/updated/removed
- Environment Variables table updated if an env var changed
- Connecting Your Inbox / Groq sections updated if those flows changed
- Run Locally still matches `requirements.txt` and the actual start command
